# ManaQuest Content Conventions

## Front matter (required)

```yaml
---
author: "Max Weber"
title: "Sharp, ≤70 chars, value-first"
date: "YYYY-MM-DD"
description: "1–2 sentence summary, includes core keyword. Used for SEO + card preview."
image: cover.png   # bundle filename OR absolute /path
tags: [kebab-case, lowercase]
keywords:           # optional, SEO boost
  - core term
  - long-tail term
ShowToc: true
ShowBreadCrumbs: true
---
```

## Page bundles (preferred for image-heavy posts)

Use `content/posts/<slug>/index.md` + sibling images. `image:` accepts bare filename — theme resolves via `Resources.GetMatch`.

```
content/posts/ldash/
  index.md
  cover.png
  portfolio.png
```

## Inline image

Single image gets pixel frame + lightbox automatically:

```md
![Alt text describing the image](portfolio.png)
```

For 2–4 images side-by-side, use the gallery shortcode (see `manaquest-components`).

## Code blocks

Always tag the language → render hook adds language label + line numbers.

````md
```rust
fn main() { println!("hello"); }
```
````

## Callouts

Use markdown blockquote — automatically styled as game-callout (✦ glyph + cyan corner):

```md
> Repo: [codeberg.org/...](https://codeberg.org/...)
```

## Links

- One link per concept. No link spam.
- External authoritative sources welcome (project homepages, ecosystem hubs).
- Internal cross-links preferred over orphaning posts (`/posts/<slug>/`).
- Always close posts with a "Stay in touch" block (YouTube, Nostr/Primal, Patreon).

## Don'ts

- No bare filenames in `tags:` — use kebab-case (`personal-development`, not `Personal Development`).
- No future `date:` unless intentionally scheduled (Hugo skips them; use `hugo -F` to preview).
- No HTML inside markdown when a shortcode or class exists.
